  <data name="DownloadButton" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Download Anti-Cheat</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq1A" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Check that the panel is green. Right after you join the server it takes a few seconds to clear you. If it is red, read the reason, close it and open it again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq1Q" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>I was moved to spectators</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq2A" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Remove skins, mods and files added to the game, and close overlay, capture or optimization programs. If it continues, verify the game files in Steam and tell the administration the message shown.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq2Q" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>An altered file or incompatible program error appeared</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq3A" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Click Continue so the game can open. Ideally, untick "Run as administrator" and compatibility mode in the steam.exe properties.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq3Q" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Steam showed a compatibility warning</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq4A" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Download the file again on this page.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq4Q" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>"New version available" appeared</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq5A" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No. The game opens with VAC off in that session (see below). Nothing changes on your account.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq5Q" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Can the Anti-Cheat get me a VAC ban?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="FaqTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Common problems</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HelpText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Still having trouble? Tell the administration the message text and the time.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="InsecureText1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Anti-Cheat opens the game with the -insecure option, which starts it without VAC. That avoids any VAC ban risk caused by the Anti-Cheat, and the l4d2.com.br server also runs without VAC.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="InsecureText2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>With the Anti-Cheat, you can only join servers without VAC, like ours. To play on a server with VAC, close the Anti-Cheat and open the game normally through Steam.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="InsecureTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>About -insecure (no VAC)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyNever1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>It does not take screenshots</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyNever2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>It does not read your documents or files outside the game</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyNever3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>It does not store your IP or write logs on your computer</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyNeverTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>What it does not do</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacySends1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your Steam ID and profile name</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacySends2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Anti-Cheat and Windows versions</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacySends3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Security and diagnostic events</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacySendsTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>What it sends</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Privacy</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Requirements" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Windows only · Left 4 Dead 2 through Steam · Asks for administrator permission</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StatusFailedLabel" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Failed</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StatusFailedText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Read the reason, close it and open the Anti-Cheat again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StatusReadyLabel" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Active</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StatusReadyText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>You are cleared to play.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StatusStartingLabel" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Starting / Waiting</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StatusStartingText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Working or waiting for your answer. Do not close it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StatusTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>What the window shows</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Step1Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Accept the administrator permission. If SmartScreen warns you, click "More info" and "Run anyway".</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Step1Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Download and run</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Step2Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pick your Steam account and, if it asks to close Steam or L4D2, type Y and Enter. The game opens and connects by itself.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Step2Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Answer and wait</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Step3Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When the green ANTI-CHEAT ACTIVE panel appears, you can play. Closing the Anti-Cheat removes your clearance.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Step3Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Play with the window open</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StepsTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>How to use it</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Subtitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Required to play on the competitive server. It opens the game, checks that everything is in order and clears you to play.</value>
